description: How to work in the pde_metrics repository
alwaysApply: true
---

The full instructions are in `AGENTS.md` at the repository root. Read it before changing
anything; it is the canonical file and this one is only a pointer, so the two cannot drift
apart.

It covers adding metrics, degradations, data sources and report renderers; the testing
conventions; how to treat generated LaTeX; and a table of traps that have already caught
someone.

Five rules that are easy to violate by accident:

- Verify before claiming. `pytest | tail` masks the exit code, so a `&&` chain passes with
  failing tests. Use
  `pytest -q > /tmp/pt.txt 2>&1; RC=$?; tail -3 /tmp/pt.txt; [ $RC -eq 0 ] || exit 1`.
- Never hand-edit anything under `results/`. It is generated; fix the renderer and re-run
  `make_report.py`.
- Define every value once. Before writing a function or constant, search for the one that
  already exists and extend it (`AGENTS.md` §1).
- Delete an issue once it is fully resolved. `issues/` holds only open items: remove the file
  and its row in `issues/README.md`, and rewrite every reference to it (`AGENTS.md` §1).
- Evaluate a metric the way its own field does, on every experiment where it makes sense.
  Build every standard where fields disagree, say on the card why any experiment was skipped,
  and write up the field's missing experiments as proposals (`AGENTS.md` §1, "How every metric
  is evaluated").
